<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hussein bin Ali, King of Hejaz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1854–1931</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sharif Hussein</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hussein bin Ali, a Hashemite, was appointed Sharif and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharif-of-mecca">Emir of Mecca</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1908. Encouraged by the Hussein–McMahon correspondence, he launched the Arab Revolt in June 1916 and proclaimed himself King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a>. His sons Faisal and Abdullah became kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and Jordan, but he lost the Hejaz to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a> in 1924–1925.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hussein-bin-ali-king-of-hejaz.jpg" alt="Hussein bin Ali, King of Hejaz" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sharif_Husayn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
